>> title: Deli Rye Bread
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, rye, caraway, yeast, oven
>> counters: Deli, Bakery
>> aka: Jewish rye, seeded rye, caraway rye
>> pairs-with: borscht
>> servings: 12
>> time: 15 hr
>> slack: narrow — rye has little gluten to hold gas, and a loaf left past an hour after shaping collapses into a dense damp band along the bottom
>> step.1: stir the rye sponge, rest 12 hours
>> step.2: mix to a stiff dough
>> step.3: knead 8 min, rise until doubled
>> step.4: shape an oval on a dusted sheet, proof 1 hour
>> step.6: brush, bake 425°F 35 min

Stir @rye flour{1%cup}(110 g), @warm water{3/4%cup}(170 g), and @instant yeast{1/4%tsp}(0.8 g) together, then rest ~{12%hours}.

Mix @&(~1)rye sponge{} with @bread flour{2 1/2%cup}(340 g), @warm water{2/3%cup}(155 g), @instant yeast{1%tsp}(3 g), @caraway seeds{1%Tbs}(7 g), @table salt{1 3/4%tsp}(10 g), and @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL).

Knead @&(~1)dough{} for ~{8%min}, then rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

Shape @&(~1)dough{} into an oval on a #baking sheet{} dusted with @cornmeal{1%Tbs}, then proof ~{1%hour}.

Simmer @cornstarch{1%tsp}(3 g), @water{1/3%cup}(80 mL) to a thin glaze, ~{2%min}.

Brush @&(~2)loaf{} with @&(~1)cornstarch glaze{} and bake at 425°F for ~{35%min}.
